  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers the x402 payment protocol, which revives HTTP 402 Payment Required for agent and machine payments: the PaymentRequired, PaymentRequirements, ResourceInfo, PaymentPayload and SettlementResponse types; the HTTP (PAYMENT-REQUIRED, PAYMENT-SIGNATURE, PAYMENT-RESPONSE), MCP and A2A transports; the authorization, upfront and escrow payment flows; the exact, upto, batch-settlement and auth-capture schemes with their EVM and SVM bindings; the facilitator /verify, /settle and /supported APIs; Bazaar discovery and extensions; and replay, amount and expiry security. It lists two version lines: x402 v2 (current) and x402 v1 (legacy, upgraded from, with deprecated SDKs), both pinned to x402-foundation/x402 at commit cb0ec5b. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out versions and the v1 to v2 upgrade, the payment flow and transports, schemes and networks, the facilitator, and security.",
